§§ `Principles 3 and 4: where in the range`

-- Item 8, loss of an arm from the shoulder, prints 60-70%.
GIVEN course IS A `A course of healing`
      reop   IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH AN `An injury`
`item 8 healing` course `re-operated` reop MEANS
    `a listed injury` 8 1 course reop (JUST `the left arm`)

-- Principle 3: normal healing is paid at the lowest rate.
#ASSERT `the rate for` (`item 8 healing` `normal healing, without infection` `re-operated` FALSE) EQUALS 60
-- Principle 4: a complicated wound is paid up to the highest rate, as assessed.
#ASSERT `the rate for` (`item 8 healing` (`complicated, infected, or leaving sequelae` 65) `re-operated` FALSE) EQUALS 65
#ASSERT `the rate for` (`item 8 healing` (`complicated, infected, or leaving sequelae` 70) `re-operated` FALSE) EQUALS 70
#ASSERT REFUSED `the rate for` (`item 8 healing` (`complicated, infected, or leaving sequelae` 71) `re-operated` FALSE) BECAUSE "the rate assessed is outside the range the table prints for the row"
#ASSERT REFUSED `the rate for` (`item 8 healing` (`complicated, infected, or leaving sequelae` 59) `re-operated` FALSE) BECAUSE "the rate assessed is outside the range the table prints for the row"

§§ `Principle 6: re-operation adds 50% of the lowest rate`

-- Item 30, loss of a foot, 40-50%: normal healing 40, plus 50% of 40 = 20, is 60.
#ASSERT `the rate for` (`a listed injury` 30 1 `normal healing, without infection` TRUE (JUST `the left leg`)) EQUALS 60
-- Complicated at 45, plus 20, is 65.
#ASSERT `the rate for` (`a listed injury` 30 1 (`complicated, infected, or leaving sequelae` 45) TRUE NOTHING) EQUALS 65
-- An unlisted injury has no printed range for principle 6 to halve.
#ASSERT `the rate for` (`an injury not listed in the table` 25 FALSE NOTHING) EQUALS 25
#ASSERT REFUSED `the rate for` (`an injury not listed in the table` 25 TRUE NOTHING) BECAUSE "principle 6 has no scale for an injury not listed in the table"

§§ `Principle 5: several injuries, the sum insured and the limb`

-- Two injuries to the left arm: item 11 (a hand, 45-55) and item 23 (stiff shoulder,
-- 30-40), both normal: 45 + 30 = 75, above the 70 for losing an arm (item 8's highest).
#ASSERT `the total rate for` (LIST `a listed injury` 11 1 `normal healing, without infection` FALSE (JUST `the left arm`), `a listed injury` 23 1 `normal healing, without infection` FALSE (JUST `the left arm`)) EQUALS 70
-- The same two injuries, one to each arm: 45 + 30 = 75, no limb cap.
#ASSERT `the total rate for` (LIST `a listed injury` 11 1 `normal healing, without infection` FALSE (JUST `the left arm`), `a listed injury` 23 1 `normal healing, without infection` FALSE (JUST `the right arm`)) EQUALS 75
-- Item 9 (55-65) and item 42 (15-20), no limb named: 55 + 15 = 70% of 100.000.000.
#ASSERT `the amount under the table on` 100000000 `for` (LIST `a listed injury` 9 1 `normal healing, without infection` FALSE NOTHING, `a listed injury` 42 1 `normal healing, without infection` FALSE NOTHING) EQUALS 70000000
-- Items 8 (60, left arm) and 27 (60, left leg): 120% is capped at the sum insured.
#ASSERT `the amount under the table on` 100000000 `for` (LIST `a listed injury` 8 1 `normal healing, without infection` FALSE (JUST `the left arm`), `a listed injury` 27 1 `normal healing, without infection` FALSE (JUST `the left leg`)) EQUALS 100000000
-- Section I, death, 100%.
#ASSERT `the amount under the table on` 50000000 `for` (LIST `a listed injury` 0 1 `normal healing, without infection` FALSE NOTHING) EQUALS 50000000
